## ABSTRACT
Inthis studyanalkynyl-modifiedaromaticdicarboxylicacidbifunctionaligandwasselectedtoconstructlanthanidecompound $\{[\mathsf{E}\mathsf{u}_{4}(\mathsf{e b d c})_{6}(4,4\mathsf{-b p y})_{0.5}(\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O})_{4.5}]\cdot(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{5}\mathsf{O}\mathsf{H})_{1.25}(\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O})\}_{n}$ (Eu-MOF, ${\mathsf{H}}_{2}{\mathsf{e b d c}}=5$ -ethynyl-isophthalic acid, $4,4\mathrm{-}\mathsf{b p y}=4,4$ -bipyridine, and ${\mathsf{M O F}}=$ metal-oganic framework),of which theuncoordinated alkynyl group would beused to anchor silver nanoclusters (Ag NCs). The Eu-MOF exhibits double emission peaks, located at 492 and $611\ \mathsf{n m}$ ， respectively, in which the high-energy blue emission isassociated withalkynyl-modifiedligandwhilethelow-energyredemissionbelongstocharacteristic emissionof $\mathsf{E u}^{3+}$ indicating that ligands can effectively sensitize $\mathsf{E u}^{3+}$ luminescence. The intensity ratio of the dual emission fluorescence peaks of Eu-MOFdisplaysagoodlinearrelationshipwithtemperature,whichrealizes thedetectionfunction inthelowtemperature region of $75{-}275~\mathsf{K}$ ，and the thermal sensitivity reaches $1.5398\%\cdot\mathsf{K}^{-1}$ . After anchoring the Ag NCs,the high-energy blue emission is significantly quenched, indicating that the ${\sf A g N C s}$ are indeed confined into the framework and interact with the alkynyl group, and thuschangetheoverallelectronicdistibution.This isthefirstcaseofanchoring Ag NCsbyaluminescent Eu-MOFand studying nanoclusterloading byusing spectroscopic properties.Inaddion,theAg NCs@Eu-MOFalsoshowsagodcatalytic activity for cycloaddition reaction from ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ and epoxides. This study not only provides ideas for exploring the changes in optical properties of luminescent MOFsand Ag NCscaused byconfinement effect,but alsoexpands their potentialapplications in various fields.
