## 3 Conclusions
In summary, for the first time, we successfully prepared a photoluminescent Eu-MOF by the method of hydrothermal synthesis, and a host-guest composite $\operatorname{Ag}\operatorname{NC}s@$ Eu-MOF in a simple and mild solution immersion way. The as-prepared EuMOF exhibits excellent temperaturedependent photoluminescence properties and great development potential in temperature sensor. In addition,with carbon dioxide involved, the obtained Ag NCs@Eu-MOF as catalysts can be efficiently converted epoxides into to cyclic carbonates, showing excellent catalytic capability. The host-guest interaction between the luminescent MOF and the guest Ag NCs is very fascinating and interesting, which will provide experimental reference and theoretical model of metal clusters@MOFs.
